Z||000000||BroCar 87||07-29-2000||10:38 PM||||Well as some of you know I just bought a 1984 SE 4 cylinder 4 speed Fiero. It only cost me $140.00, because he doesn't have the title. I did the lemon check deal on the internet, and nothing about being stolen or any fires came up.<BR>So I am thinking, I should drag race this one. I already have a daily street driver, and I LOVE to race. <BR>I did some research and found a body type that I want to use instead of the Fiero body. DON'T get me wrong, I LOVE the notchback's and GT's. At the track, I want something that is gonna STAND OUT more though!<BR>A buddy of mine build's 4 cylinder race engines. I mean he goes all out! <BR>So my thoughts are to get the engine done first, and then get the body kit. I was looking for a kit that just replaced the fiero body with out stretching the chassis, like sooooo many I have seen. So I want to get the MIRAGE K from EURO-WORKS. I gave them an email, and told them about my idea. They replied the next day (today), and said they would help me out. MAY EVEN SPONSOR ME!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>So now, I am all joyous inside and can't wait to get this underway. Not to mention tell ALLL my friends about this. So anyways, you all are the first to know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I WILL KEEP EVERYONE POSTED!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000001||KnightRyder31||07-29-2000||10:54 PM||||I'm glad to see that your so happy....I would be too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> . But one thing, if you went to a drag strip, or a track with a stock looking fiero...I think you will get all the eyes you need. Hell, if you go to the track or strip with a fiero period...you will catch a lot of eyes. Also, it would be a great sleeper!||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||07-30-2000||12:36 PM||||YEA KnightRyder, it WOULD make a great sleeper and would attract many eyes, but the thing is, HERE is something that not everyone is offered. SPONSORSHIP! So... that caught me in a heartbeat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> . Thanks for such a quick reply,<BR>BroCar 87<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||07-30-2000||01:50 PM||||Hey Brocar here is something else I learned today for our area..by the end of the year, we will have someone performing the V8 conversion kits right here in our area.     They have the cradle already molded for it and they have got alot of input form Chris the guy that had that sweet red V8 that :Jeff(BBBadGT)just bought. refer to post about new v8 fiero on this list. The cost will not be as high as others either. We will have to see final project but looks promising. will keep you up to date!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> And did you know there is a Northstar powered GT in OP ? I found it yesterday! A little problem with the axles but a VERY sweet car. <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||1
